<title>UK: UK will not refer Boeing buy of Rockwell unit.</title>
<headline>UK will not refer Boeing buy of Rockwell unit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The UK Department of Trade and Industry said on Wednesday that it would not be referring the purchase by Boeing Co of some assets of Rockwell International Corp to the Monopolies and Mergers Commission.</p>
<p>U.S.-based Rockwell, which is now mainly a commercial electronics firm, sold its aerospace and defence businesses to U.S. aircraft giant Boeing for $3.2 billion in December 1996.</p>
<p>- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
